---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.BrokenTestRow
---@field fingerprint string Stable identity of this distinct failure: the failing test's node id plus a normalized error signature, so the same failure across runs groups into one row.
---@field test_id string The pytest node id from the CI 'FAILED <id>' line: the failing test.
---@field error_signature string The trailing failure detail with volatile bits (numbers, hashes) normalized, shared across runs of the same failure. Empty when the FAILED line carried no detail.
---@field job_name string The CI job the failure most recently came from. Matched against default-branch job status to decide whether trunk is currently broken by it.
---@field repo string 'owner/name' repository the failure belongs to.
---@field state posthog.engineering_analytics.BrokenTestStateEnum The classifier's verdict on how this failure is behaving right now: 'breaking_master' (failing on trunk, latest trunk run still red), 'blocking_merge_queue' (stopped a merge on a commit that already passed the PR's own CI, trunk still green), 'novel_burst' (new within a day and spreading across branches, not on trunk yet), 'potentially_resolved' (hit trunk but trunk is green again), 'flaky' (sporadic across branches over more than a day), or 'pr_only' (confined to one branch: one PR's own problem). * `breaking_master` - Breaking Master * `blocking_merge_queue` - Blocking Merge Queue * `novel_burst` - Novel Burst * `potentially_resolved` - Potentially Resolved * `flaky` - Flaky * `pr_only` - PR Only
---@field first_seen string Earliest failure line for this fingerprint in the analysis window.
---@field last_seen string Most recent failure line for this fingerprint in the analysis window.
---@field occurrences number Total failure lines for this fingerprint in the window. An absolute count, never a rate: passing runs aren't in this data.
---@field branches number Distinct branches the failure appeared on in the window.
---@field master_hits number Failure lines on the default branch (master/main). 0 means it never reached trunk.
---@field latest_run_id number The most recent failing workflow run for this fingerprint: pass it to run_failure_logs to fetch the actual failing log lines.
---@field latest_branch string The branch of the most recent failing run.
---@field trend_24h? posthog.engineering_analytics.BrokenTestRowTrend24hList Hourly failure counts over the last 24 hours, oldest first (fixed 24-slot array), for the row sparkline. All zeros when nothing failed in the last day.
---@field latest_ci_engine? posthog.engineering_analytics.CIEngineEnum|distilled.Null CI execution engine; null when unknown. * `github_actions` - GitHub Actions * `depot_ci` - Depot CI

---Hourly failure counts over the last 24 hours, oldest first (fixed 24-slot array), for the row sparkline. All zeros when nothing failed in the last day.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.BrokenTestRowTrend24hList number[]

