---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.DeliveryStageTiming
---@field stage posthog.engineering_analytics.DeliveryStageEnum Which leg this is: 'open_to_gate' (created_at to the PR's first merge-queue gate run starting) or 'gate_to_merge' (that gate run to merged_at). The post-merge leg is the DORA endpoint's median_merge_to_deploy_seconds. * `open_to_gate` - Open To Gate * `gate_to_merge` - Gate To Merge
---@field median_seconds number|distilled.Null Median seconds for this leg. Null when no PR in the window has both of its bounds observed.
---@field p90_seconds number|distilled.Null 90th-percentile seconds for this leg. Null when not observed.
---@field pr_count number PRs behind this leg's figures: those with an observed gate run. A PR that skipped the merge queue has no gate legs, so read a median against this count, not merged_pr_count.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.DeliverySummary
---@field cost_per_merged_pr_usd posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Median estimated CI cost per merged PR, in USD, over every run linked to the PR (merge-queue gate runs included) that started up to 30 days before the window. Null when the jobs table isn't synced.
---@field billable_minutes_per_merged_pr posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Median billable runner minutes per merged PR, on the billed clock. Null when the jobs table isn't synced.
---@field cost_per_push_usd posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Total CI cost divided by total pushes over the merged PRs: the price of one iteration. A push is a distinct head commit that triggered CI.
---@field median_ready_to_merge_seconds posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Median seconds from the last ready_for_review to merge. Null when issue events aren't synced.
---@field p90_ready_to_merge_seconds posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure 90th percentile of the ready-to-merge seconds.
---@field median_ready_to_first_approval_seconds posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Median seconds from ready to the first approval. An approval given while the PR was a draft counts as 0. PRs merged without an approval are left out. Null when reviews aren't synced.
---@field median_first_approval_to_merge_seconds posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Median seconds from the first approval to merge. This median and the one before it do not add up to the ready-to-merge median.
---@field before_first_approval_share posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Share (0 to 1) of all ready-to-merge hours spent before the first approval, summed over the PRs, so long PRs weigh more. The rest came after the approval.
---@field pushes_after_approval_per_merged_pr posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Mean pushes after the first approval per merged PR, over PRs with an approval.
---@field merge_queue_attempts_per_merged_pr posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Mean merge-queue gate attempts per merged PR that went through the queue. A bisection probe folds into its attempt.
---@field failed_merge_queue_share posthog.engineering_analytics.ScopeRepoFigure Share (0 to 1) of queue-landed merged PRs with at least one failed gate attempt. A failure caused by another PR ahead in the queue also counts, because the queue history is not in the warehouse.
---@field lead_time posthog.engineering_analytics.DeliveryLeadTime Lead time to deploy for the scope against the repository.
---@field scope_kind posthog.engineering_analytics.DeliveryScopeKindEnum What the read covers: 'author' (one GitHub login), 'github_team' (the members of one GitHub team, through the team membership table), or 'pull_request' (one pull request). * `author` - Author * `github_team` - GitHub Team * `pull_request` - Pull Request
---@field scope string The GitHub login or GitHub team slug the summary is for.
---@field has_membership_data boolean True when the team membership table is synced. A github_team scope without it matches no pull requests, so every scope figure is empty rather than the whole repository.
---@field jobs_available boolean True when the workflow jobs table is synced, which cost needs.
---@field review_data_available boolean True when the reviews table is synced, which the approval split needs.
---@field ready_data_available boolean True when issue events are synced, which ready-to-merge time needs.
---@field opened_pr_count number PRs in scope opened in the window, drafts included, bots excluded.
---@field merged_pr_count number PRs in scope merged in the window (bots and drafts excluded): the population of every per-merged-PR figure.
---@field open_pr_count number PRs in scope that are open and not drafts right now. Ignores the window.
---@field draft_pr_count number PRs in scope that are open drafts right now. Ignores the window.
---@field total_cost_usd number|distilled.Null Estimated CI cost summed over the merged PRs in scope. Null when nothing was costable.
---@field total_billable_minutes number|distilled.Null Billable minutes summed over the merged PRs in scope. Null when the jobs table isn't synced.
---@field push_count number Pushes summed over the merged PRs in scope.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.DeploymentFrequencyBucket
---@field bucket_start string Bucket start, aligned to series_granularity (top of hour, midnight, or Monday).
---@field deployment_count number Deployments whose first success status landed in this bucket, within the environment scope. Zero-filled: 0 means nothing shipped.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.DepotCIRepoUsage
---@field repo string Repository the Depot source syncs, as lowercase 'owner/name'.
---@field elapsed_seconds number Run time of the finished Depot CI job attempts that started in the window, hand-off jobs included.
---@field estimated_cost_usd number elapsed_seconds at the Depot CI list price for a 2-vCPU sandbox. Depot does not report the sandbox size of an attempt.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverview
---@field deployment_frequency_series posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewDeploymentFrequencySeriesList Successful deployments per bucket across the window, oldest first, zero-filled, bucketed by series_granularity. Empty when the deploy tables aren't synced.
---@field merge_to_deploy_series posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewMergeToDeploySeriesList Merge-to-deploy distribution per bucket across the window, oldest first: the box-plot series (min/p5/p25/p50/mean/p75/p95/max seconds per bucket). Empty when the deploy tables aren't synced, or when github_team was passed without membership data synced.
---@field open_to_merge_series posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewOpenToMergeSeriesList Open-to-merge distribution over the SAME deployed PRs and buckets as merge_to_deploy_series, so the two stages compare bucket by bucket. Not the all-merged-PRs cycle time. Empty in the same cases as merge_to_deploy_series.
---@field open_to_deploy_series posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewOpenToDeploySeriesList Open-to-deploy distribution over the same deployed PRs and buckets: the full open to first-successful-deploy span the two stages above compose into. Empty in the same cases as merge_to_deploy_series.
---@field deploy_data_available boolean False when the deployments/deployment_statuses tables aren't synced for the selected repo; every other field is then empty or null, never a fake zero.
---@field environment_scope string Display label for the selected environments, comma-separated, 'persistent' when no persistent environments were discovered. Use selected_environments for exact names.
---@field environments posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewEnvironmentsList Distinct persistent environments from the metric scan window or the 30 days before its end, whichever starts earlier, most-deployed first. Transient environments are omitted.
---@field selected_environments posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewSelectedEnvironmentsList Exact environment names used for these metrics. Defaults to all persistent environments marked production or named prod/production (including regional suffixes), falling back to the busiest persistent environment. Explicit filters are trimmed and deduplicated. DRF rejects blank or unknown names; real transient names are allowed.
---@field has_membership_data boolean True when the optional team-membership snapshot is synced. When false, a github_team filter cannot be honored and the merge-to-deploy figures go empty rather than silently unfiltered.
---@field github_teams posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewGithubTeamsList Distinct GitHub team slugs from the membership snapshot, sorted: the team picker's options. Empty when membership isn't synced.
---@field deployment_count number Deployments whose first success status landed in the window, within the environment scope.
---@field deployment_count_prev number Same count over the equal-length window before date_from.
---@field deployments_per_day number|distilled.Null deployment_count normalized by the window length in days. Null only when the deploy tables aren't synced.
---@field deployments_per_day_prev number|distilled.Null Previous-window twin of deployments_per_day. Null only when the deploy tables aren't synced.
---@field median_merge_to_deploy_seconds number|distilled.Null Median seconds from a PR's merge to the first successful deployment containing it (bots/drafts excluded; narrowed by github_team when given). Containment is resolved through the deploy's head commit, not the deploy's success time. Keyed on deploy time. This is merge-to-deploy, not full commit-to-deploy DORA lead time. Null when nothing deployed in the window.
---@field median_merge_to_deploy_seconds_prev number|distilled.Null Previous-window twin of median_merge_to_deploy_seconds.
---@field median_open_to_deploy_seconds number|distilled.Null Median seconds from a PR's open to the first successful deployment containing it: the full open-to-deploy lead time over the same deployed-PR population as median_merge_to_deploy_seconds. Null when nothing deployed in the window.
---@field median_open_to_deploy_seconds_prev number|distilled.Null Previous-window twin of median_open_to_deploy_seconds.
---@field deployed_pr_count number PRs first deployed in the window: the population behind the merge-to-deploy median and box plot.
---@field deployed_pr_count_prev number Previous-window twin of deployed_pr_count.
---@field failed_deployment_count number Deployments with at least one failure/error status, keyed on the first failure time.
---@field failed_deployment_count_prev number Previous-window twin of failed_deployment_count.
---@field failed_deployment_share number|distilled.Null Failed deployments over deployments that reached any outcome (success or failure). A change-failure proxy: no incident data is linked, so a deploy that succeeded but broke production is not counted. Null when nothing reached an outcome.
---@field failed_deployment_share_prev number|distilled.Null Previous-window twin of failed_deployment_share.
---@field median_failed_deploy_to_next_success_seconds number|distilled.Null Median seconds from a deployment's first failure status to the next successful deployment in the same environment. A time-to-restore proxy: recovery by anything other than a deploy is invisible, and failures not yet recovered are excluded. Null when no failed deploy recovered in the window.
---@field median_failed_deploy_to_next_success_seconds_prev number|distilled.Null Previous-window twin of median_failed_deploy_to_next_success_seconds.
---@field merged_pr_count number PRs merged in the window (bots and drafts excluded; narrowed by github_team when given): the denominator behind unattributed_merged_pr_share.
---@field unattributed_merged_pr_share number|distilled.Null Share of merged_pr_count no successful in-scope deployment attributed: recent merges still waiting for their deploy, plus merges whose deploy the scope or scan bounds miss. Null when nothing merged in the window.
---@field latest_deploy_status_at string|distilled.Null The newest deployment status row synced, any environment: how fresh the deploy data is. Windows ending after this instant undercount. Null when the deploy tables are empty.
---@field series_granularity string Bucket width of every series: the granularity param when given, else chosen to fit the window: 'hour', 'day', or 'week'.

---Successful deployments per bucket across the window, oldest first, zero-filled, bucketed by series_granularity. Empty when the deploy tables aren't synced.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewDeploymentFrequencySeriesList posthog.engineering_analytics.DeploymentFrequencyBucket[]

---Distinct persistent environments from the metric scan window or the 30 days before its end, whichever starts earlier, most-deployed first. Transient environments are omitted.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewEnvironmentsList string[]

---Distinct GitHub team slugs from the membership snapshot, sorted: the team picker's options. Empty when membership isn't synced.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewGithubTeamsList string[]

---Merge-to-deploy distribution per bucket across the window, oldest first: the box-plot series (min/p5/p25/p50/mean/p75/p95/max seconds per bucket). Empty when the deploy tables aren't synced, or when github_team was passed without membership data synced.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewMergeToDeploySeriesList posthog.engineering_analytics.LeadTimeBucket[]

---Open-to-deploy distribution over the same deployed PRs and buckets: the full open to first-successful-deploy span the two stages above compose into. Empty in the same cases as merge_to_deploy_series.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewOpenToDeploySeriesList posthog.engineering_analytics.LeadTimeBucket[]

---Open-to-merge distribution over the SAME deployed PRs and buckets as merge_to_deploy_series, so the two stages compare bucket by bucket. Not the all-merged-PRs cycle time. Empty in the same cases as merge_to_deploy_series.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewOpenToMergeSeriesList posthog.engineering_analytics.LeadTimeBucket[]

---Exact environment names used for these metrics. Defaults to all persistent environments marked production or named prod/production (including regional suffixes), falling back to the busiest persistent environment. Explicit filters are trimmed and deduplicated. DRF rejects blank or unknown names; real transient names are allowed.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.DoraOverviewSelectedEnvironmentsList string[]

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.DurationDistribution
---@field pr_count number Pull requests in the distribution. Every statistic is null when this is 0.
---@field min_seconds number|distilled.Null Fastest duration, in seconds.
---@field p05_seconds number|distilled.Null 5th percentile, in seconds: the lower whisker.
---@field p25_seconds number|distilled.Null 25th percentile, in seconds: the box's lower edge.
---@field p50_seconds number|distilled.Null Median, in seconds.
---@field mean_seconds number|distilled.Null Mean, in seconds.
---@field p75_seconds number|distilled.Null 75th percentile, in seconds: the box's upper edge.
---@field p95_seconds number|distilled.Null 95th percentile, in seconds: the upper whisker.
---@field max_seconds number|distilled.Null Slowest duration, in seconds.

