---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.EngineeringAnalyticsFlakyTestsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field branch? string Optional exact branch name. Keeps only tests that failed on it, but the counts still cover every branch, so a row shows whether the test also fails elsewhere. Applied before the limit.
---@field date_from? string Window start: relative ('-7d', '-30d') or ISO8601. Defaults to -7d; the window may span at most 30 days.
---@field date_to? string Window end: relative or ISO8601. Defaults to now.
---@field limit? number Maximum number of tests to return (1-200). Defaults to 50.
---@field min_failed_prs? number A test with no recorded recovery qualifies once it failed on at least this many distinct pull requests in the window. Minimum 1. Defaults to 3.
---@field pr_number? number Optional pull request number. Keeps only tests that failed in that PR's CI runs, but the counts still cover every PR. Pass min_failed_prs=1 too, so a test that failed on this PR alone qualifies. Applied before the limit.
---@field repo? string 'owner/name' repository to scope to when the selected source syncs several repositories (from the `sources` list). Defaults to the source's first repository.
---@field runner? posthog.engineering_analytics.EngineeringAnalyticsFlakyTestsRequestRunner|string Optional test runner to return: 'pytest' or 'jest'.
---@field source_id? string Connected GitHub data warehouse source to read from. Defaults to the oldest connected GitHub source that the `sources` list reports as synced, when the team has more than one.
---@field test? string Optional case-insensitive substring of the test id to keep, e.g. 'test_cohort' or 'posthog/api/test/test_user.py'. Applied before the limit, so a test past the cap is still found.

---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.EngineeringAnalyticsFlakyTestsRequestRunner "jest"|"pytest"

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.EngineeringAnalyticsJobAggregatesRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field branch? string Optional exact git branch (head_branch) to scope results to, e.g. 'main'. Omit or leave blank to aggregate across all branches.
---@field date_from? string Window start: relative ('-30d', '-8w') or ISO8601. Defaults to -30d.
---@field date_to? string Window end: relative or ISO8601. Defaults to now.
