---* `confirmed_flake` - Confirmed Flake
---* `suspected_regression` - Suspected Regression
---* `quarantined` - Quarantined
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestClassificationEnum "confirmed_flake"|"suspected_regression"|"quarantined"

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestItem
---@field runner posthog.engineering_analytics.CITestRunnerEnum Test runner that emitted this signal: 'pytest' or 'jest'. * `pytest` - Pytest * `jest` - Jest
---@field nodeid string Runner-specific stable test identity (the CI span name). This is a grouping key, not necessarily runnable; use `selector` to run or quarantine the test.
---@field selector string Runnable pytest or Jest selector. Exact when the CI reporter emitted it; older pytest spans use a best-effort reconstruction from the nodeid.
---@field classification posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestClassificationEnum confirmed_flake: one commit both failed and passed the test (a re-run attempt went green, or an in-job retry recovered it), so it is provably nondeterministic. quarantined: a tolerated failure was recorded while it was masked. suspected_regression: only failures were recorded, which is absence of proof, not proof that it is a real break. * `confirmed_flake` - Confirmed Flake * `suspected_regression` - Suspected Regression * `quarantined` - Quarantined
---@field same_commit_recovery_run_count number Runs where one commit both failed and passed the test: a 'Re-run failed jobs' attempt went green on the same commit, or an in-job pytest retry (tests hand-marked @pytest.mark.flaky(reruns=N)) recovered it. A pass in a different run is a different commit and never counts.
---@field failed_run_count number Distinct CI runs whose recorded outcome was failed or error. A run counts once however many matrix legs it failed in.
---@field failed_pr_count number Distinct pull requests among the failed runs. Failures on master or unattributed branches carry no PR number and are excluded here (still in failed_run_count).
---@field master_failed_run_count number Failed runs on the default branch (master/main approximation): the 'matters right now' signal that a test is breaking the trunk, not just PR branches.
---@field quarantined_failed_run_count number Runs where the test recorded a tolerated failure while quarantined: already masked in CI, still failing.
---@field last_signal_at string Most recent failure, recovery, or quarantined-failure run for this test in the window.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestList
---@field items posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestListItemsList Tests worth acting on now, ranked by blast radius: master failures, then PRs hit, then runs. A CI setup break (a run attempt whose tests errored in 3 or more jobs or for 3 or more owning teams, or a job attempt with 100 or more distinct failed or errored tests) excludes every trial of that attempt, not only its failures.
---@field truncated boolean True when more tests qualified than the cap; `items` is the highest-ranked `limit` rows.
---@field limit number Maximum number of tests returned in `items`.

---Tests worth acting on now, ranked by blast radius: master failures, then PRs hit, then runs. A CI setup break (a run attempt whose tests errored in 3 or more jobs or for 3 or more owning teams, or a job attempt with 100 or more distinct failed or errored tests) excludes every trial of that attempt, not only its failures.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestListItemsList posthog.engineering_analytics.FlakyTestItem[]

