---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamCIHealthItem
---@field owner_team string Owning team slug from the repo's owners.yaml map (e.g. 'team-replay'), or the literal 'unowned' for tests whose spans carry no ownership stamp.
---@field flaky_test_count number Owned tests one commit was seen both failing and passing in the window: the same proof, and the same word, that flaky_tests calls a confirmed_flake. Compare with flaky_test_count_prior for the delta.
---@field flaky_test_count_prior number Same count over the equal-length window immediately before date_from.
---@field regression_test_count number Owned tests that failed with no recorded same-commit recovery and still hit the blast-radius bar (a master/main failure, or min_failed_prs distinct PRs). Not flakes: absence of proof, not proof.
---@field regression_test_count_prior number Same count over the prior window.
---@field failed_run_count number Distinct CI runs where at least one owned test failed or errored. A run with many failing owned tests counts once. An absolute count, not a rate: fast passing runs are not emitted.
---@field failed_run_count_prior number Same count over the prior window.
---@field same_commit_recovery_run_count number Distinct CI runs where one commit both failed and passed at least one owned test: a re-run attempt went green, or an in-job retry recovered it.
---@field same_commit_recovery_run_count_prior number Same count over the prior window.
---@field quarantined_failed_run_count number Distinct CI runs where at least one owned test recorded a tolerated failure while quarantined.
---@field quarantined_failed_run_count_prior number Same count over the prior window.
---@field last_seen_at string|distilled.Null Most recent failure, recovery, or quarantined-failure run across the team's owned tests, either window. Null for a team present only through the census (no CI signal recorded).
---@field test_file_count? number|distilled.Null Test files the team owns per the daily owners.yaml census. Null until a census event exists for the repository.
---@field test_file_count_prior? number|distilled.Null The latest census value at or before the window start, for the trend.
---@field merged_pr_count? number|distilled.Null Merged PRs authored by the team's members in the window, bots excluded. Null when the team_members snapshot isn't synced, or for 'unowned'.
---@field merged_pr_count_prior? number|distilled.Null Same count over the prior window.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamCIHealthList
---@field items posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamCIHealthListItemsList Owning teams ranked by current flaky + failure signal, heaviest first, capped at `limit`. Teams are organizational owners of code surfaces; this never aggregates by author. A CI setup break (a run attempt whose tests errored in 3 or more jobs or for 3 or more owning teams, or a job attempt with 100 or more distinct failed or errored tests) excludes every trial of that attempt, not only its failures.
---@field truncated boolean True when more teams had signal than the cap.
---@field limit number Maximum number of teams returned in `items`.

---Owning teams ranked by current flaky + failure signal, heaviest first, capped at `limit`. Teams are organizational owners of code surfaces; this never aggregates by author. A CI setup break (a run attempt whose tests errored in 3 or more jobs or for 3 or more owning teams, or a job attempt with 100 or more distinct failed or errored tests) excludes every trial of that attempt, not only its failures.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamCIHealthListItemsList posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamCIHealthItem[]

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamFriction
---@field github_team string GitHub team slug.
---@field median_score number The median friction of the team's scored members, in 'x typical' units.
---@field scored_author_count number Members with enough merged pull requests to score. A team shows only above a floor, so one or two people never read as a team's figure.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamMergeTrend
---@field points posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamMergeTrendPointsList Daily median and average open→merge over the PRs this team's members merged, ascending by day. Coarse timing (open→merge combines draft and review time); bots excluded.
---@field owner_team string The team slug this trend is scoped to.
---@field has_membership_data boolean False when the GitHub source has no team_members snapshot synced: the trend then has no honest team attribution and `points` is empty.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamMergeTrendPoint
---@field day string Start of the day bucket (team timezone), keyed on merged_at.
---@field median_seconds number|distilled.Null Median open→merge seconds of the PRs this team's members merged that day; null on a day the team merged nothing.
---@field average_seconds number|distilled.Null Average open→merge seconds over the same merges; diverges above the median when a few long-running PRs drag the mean. Null on a day the team merged nothing.
---@field merged_count number Merged PRs behind that day's median and average.

---Daily median and average open→merge over the PRs this team's members merged, ascending by day. Coarse timing (open→merge combines draft and review time); bots excluded.
---@alias posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamMergeTrendPointsList posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamMergeTrendPoint[]

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamReadyToMergeMedians
---@field medians posthog.engineering_analytics.ReadyToMergeMedians|distilled.Null Over the pull requests by the team's members, the same population as a github_team scope, without the pr_number pull request. Null when fewer than three other authors contribute a ready time, because the author could read a teammate's value back from the median. The approval medians are null on the same terms for approvals.
---@field github_team string The GitHub team slug.

---@class posthog.engineering_analytics.TeamTestSignal
